  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Image validation results\n- Breaking: ImageValidationResult is now a union of ValidImageResult and InvalidImageResult rather than a record with shared metadata and errors.\n- Pattern-match valid results for detected Format, Width, Height, FileSizeBytes, and original encoded Bytes. Invalid results expose Errors and SuggestedScaling.\n- IsValid and ThrowIfInvalid() remain available on the union.\n- Replaced string errors with NotASupportedImageError for non-image, undecodable, or unsupported contents and ImageSizeExceededError exposing the maximum encoded file size. Both support GetErrorMessage().\n- Fixed undersized width and height validation messages to report that the dimension is too small.\n\nImage asset integration\n- Image helpers now construct ImageAsset with bytes through the FileData API instead of the obsolete FromByteArray factory.\n- Validation and automatic adjustment helpers handle the valid and invalid result cases. Resized output remains PNG and is not revalidated.",
